cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below and cite the data sets listed in docs/DATA.md."
title: "QEC-Leakage-Tracker: a label-free leakage tracker for surface-code decoding"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yiannosste/QEC-Leakage-Tracker"
url: "https://github.com/Yiannosste/QEC-Leakage-Tracker"
authors:
  - family-names: "Stergiou"
    given-names: "Ioannis"
    affiliation: "School of Electrical and Computer Engineering, National Technical University of Athens, Greece"
abstract: >-
  A hidden Markov model per data qubit that reads only surface-code syndromes and estimates, per shot and per
  round, how likely each data qubit is to be leaked (or in a long-lived state that scrambles its neighbouring
  checks). The estimates become soft edge weights for minimum-weight perfect matching. The parameters are
  fitted label-free by Baum-Welch on the device's own syndromes. The repository holds the simulation studies,
  a pre-registered positive result on IBM ibm_berlin stability data, three real-data null results, and the
  cases where the tracker fails.
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - surface code
  - leakage
  - hidden Markov model
  - minimum-weight perfect matching
